<span id="Description"></span>
== Descrição ==

[[File:Std_LinkUnlink.svg|16px]] [[Std_LinkUnlink|Std LinkUnlink]] is essentially the opposite operation to [[File:Std_LinkReplace.svg|16px]] [[Std_LinkReplace|Std LinkReplace]].

This operation is used to remove a Link from a container like [[File:Std_Part.svg|16px]] [[Std_Part|Std Part]], and instead place the original object inside.

<span id="Usage"></span>
== Utilização ==

# Make sure you have a Link that is inside a container, for example, a Link to a [[File:Part_Sphere.svg|16px]] [[Part_Sphere|Part Sphere]] inside a [[File:Std_Part.svg|16px]] [[Std_Part|Std Part]].
# Select the internal Link in the [[Tree_View|Tree View]].
# There are several ways to invoke the command:
#* Press the {{Button|[[File:Std_LinkUnlink.svg|16px]] [[Std_LinkUnlink|Unlink]]}} button.
#* Select the {{MenuCommand|Edit → Create → Link Actions → [[Image:Std_LinkUnlink.svg|16px]] Unlink}} option from the menu. {{Version|26.3}}

The original [[File:Part_Sphere.svg|16px]] [[Part_Sphere|Sphere]] must now be inside the [[File:Std_Part.svg|16px]] [[Std_Part|Std Part]], and the Link must be outside. Now this Link can be deleted if it's no longer needed, and it won't break the container.

